What is the output of the following Python code?

```python
class A:
    def __init__(self):
        self.value = 5

class B(A):
    def __init__(self):
        super().__init__()
        self.value += 5

b = B()
print(b.value)
```

What is the output of the following Python code?

```python
class Meta(type):
    def __new__(cls, name, bases, dct):
        dct['x'] = 42
        return super().__new__(cls, name, bases, dct)

class MyClass(metaclass=Meta):
    pass

obj = MyClass()
print(obj.x)
```

